WEBVTT

00:00:04.919 --> 00:00:06.325
[laughs]

00:00:06.430 --> 00:00:08.089
All right! Looking good!
[Jojo giggles]

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:12.600
Okay.

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:15.460
You said you wanted to help
people in real trouble, right?

00:00:16.339 --> 00:00:17.339
Well, that's what you're doing.

00:00:17.464 --> 00:00:21.614
Blue alien hedgehogs
still count as people.
Right?

00:00:21.614 --> 00:00:22.540
I think so too.
Yeah.

00:00:22.540 --> 00:00:23.700
I think.
Okay.

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:26.299
I love you.
Did I tell you that
already?

00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:27.839
I don't deserve you.
You know that?

00:00:28.439 --> 00:00:29.439
I know that.

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:35.240
So, you're supposed to be
Tom's best friend

00:00:35.240 --> 00:00:36.340
that he won't shut up about.

00:00:36.465 --> 00:00:38.456
[panting]

00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:39.860
Well, I don't see the appeal.

00:00:41.660 --> 00:00:42.660
[laughing] Stop!

00:00:43.438 --> 00:00:44.938
That is very gross.

00:00:47.290 --> 00:00:48.290
Hey.
Hey.

00:00:48.350 --> 00:00:51.610
So, my truck still runs,
but it's pretty much totaled.

00:00:51.790 --> 00:00:53.469
You think your sister would
mind if we borrowed her car?

00:00:53.688 --> 00:00:55.068
You have got to be kidding me!

00:00:56.450 --> 00:00:58.450
She'll be fine.
Yeah, let's do that.

00:00:58.559 --> 00:01:00.048
Mm-hmm.

00:01:00.157 --> 00:01:02.482
This is my house!

00:01:02.591 --> 00:01:04.480
[horn honking]
[Sonic] Coming through!

00:01:04.590 --> 00:01:06.849
Whoa, whoa! Now this is my turn,
and I go around you.

00:01:07.170 --> 00:01:08.330
Sorry! And...

00:01:08.950 --> 00:01:11.110
perfect park.
[man] What are you, crazy?

00:01:11.469 --> 00:01:12.490
Is there anything
you didn't hit?

00:01:12.650 --> 00:01:14.349
Why did we let the alien drive?

00:01:14.410 --> 00:01:17.150
Hey, I got us here.
And please, five stars.

00:01:18.809 --> 00:01:22.050
So, this is it?
That's it. That's your pyramid.

00:01:22.690 --> 00:01:24.690
[Sonic] Wow, look at that thing!

00:01:24.710 --> 00:01:25.710
What happens now?

00:01:27.330 --> 00:01:30.028
Oh. He's... gone.
Yep.

00:01:30.210 --> 00:01:32.849
No good.
You need a special key
to get to the roof.

00:01:33.990 --> 00:01:34.990
What now?

00:01:35.790 --> 00:01:38.710
Time for me to abuse
the power entrusted to me.

00:01:48.790 --> 00:01:51.190
We got a jumper on the roof.
Gotta get up there fast

00:01:51.190 --> 00:01:52.630
or we're gonna have
a human pancake on our hands.

00:01:53.750 --> 00:01:55.568
You came all the way
from Montana.

00:01:56.750 --> 00:01:58.210
Yeah. That's how serious it is.

00:02:03.037 --> 00:02:04.057
Okay.

00:02:05.688 --> 00:02:06.969
You just saved a life.

00:02:16.090 --> 00:02:18.410
[Sonic] How much longer?
I can't breathe in here.

00:02:21.010 --> 00:02:22.889
Hello?
Anybody there?

00:02:23.450 --> 00:02:25.050
Do you have your child
in that bag?

00:02:25.809 --> 00:02:26.809
No.

00:02:27.030 --> 00:02:28.950
I mean, yes, it's a child,
but it's not mine.

00:02:30.510 --> 00:02:31.510
It's not your child.

00:02:32.389 --> 00:02:33.690
Relax.
I'm a cop, okay?

00:02:34.510 --> 00:02:35.889
Plus, he likes it in there,
don't you, buddy?

00:02:36.190 --> 00:02:37.469
[Sonic] Why would I
like it in here?

00:02:37.550 --> 00:02:39.990
This is worse than the dog cage
you had me in earlier.

00:02:41.150 --> 00:02:42.150
Such a kidder.
[laughs]

00:02:45.290 --> 00:02:46.648
[Maddie] Okay.
No, I'm scared of the dark!

00:02:47.330 --> 00:02:48.330
Is anybody there?

00:02:59.305 --> 00:03:01.083
[coughing]

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:03.580
[groans] What were you
keeping in this bag?

00:03:03.760 --> 00:03:05.478
A jar of pickled farts?

00:03:05.660 --> 00:03:06.978
All right.
What are we looking for?

00:03:10.599 --> 00:03:11.599
[ring chimes]
This.

00:03:13.119 --> 00:03:14.499
Okay.
What happens now?

00:03:14.660 --> 00:03:16.539
Now all I have to do
is think of where I want

00:03:16.539 --> 00:03:18.660
the other end of the ring
to appear, and I throw it.

00:03:18.700 --> 00:03:20.679
So that's it?
We did it?

00:03:20.879 --> 00:03:22.039
Yeah. We did it!

00:03:22.799 --> 00:03:26.019
Hey. Sorry we didn't
get to do everything
on your bucket list, pal.

00:03:26.499 --> 00:03:28.898
It's okay.
I did the ones
I needed the most.

00:03:30.259 --> 00:03:32.879
[chuckles]
You two are so cute.

00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:35.079
Oh, please. What?
We are not.

00:03:35.099 --> 00:03:36.099
No.
We're not cute.

00:03:36.099 --> 00:03:39.459
We are a couple of loose cannons
just living by our own rules.

00:03:39.459 --> 00:03:40.160
Exactly.

00:03:40.160 --> 00:03:41.160
[Maddie] Really?
[Tom] Yeah.

00:03:41.179 --> 00:03:44.280
And our rules include
expressing heartfelt emotions.

00:03:44.459 --> 00:03:45.459
If you say so.

00:03:45.938 --> 00:03:48.499
Okay, then.
All right.

00:03:49.780 --> 00:03:51.579
Um, you gotta go, right?
[Sonic] Yeah, I gotta go.

00:03:51.579 --> 00:03:52.900
I gotta go.
We gotta go too.

00:03:53.259 --> 00:03:54.259
See-- All right, bye-bye.

00:03:58.790 --> 00:04:00.490
Just one more thing.

00:04:08.490 --> 00:04:10.729
I'm sorry I was so hard on you.

00:04:13.240 --> 00:04:16.080
I know it's a tough decision
for you to leave Green Hills.

00:04:16.859 --> 00:04:19.279
Walking away from
something you care about

00:04:19.840 --> 00:04:21.000
has to be painful.

00:04:21.800 --> 00:04:23.300
You're not sure
you really want to go, huh?

00:04:24.460 --> 00:04:27.519
I don't want to go,
but I can't stay.

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:30.559
As long as I'm here,
I put everyone in danger.

00:04:31.280 --> 00:04:32.360
I can't do that.

00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:37.320
I just want you to know that
these last two days have been

00:04:37.320 --> 00:04:40.240
the best two days of my life.

00:04:43.490 --> 00:04:45.090
You know, I never
thought I'd say this,

00:04:45.170 --> 00:04:46.810
but I'm actually
gonna miss you,
you little blue devil.

00:04:47.750 --> 00:04:49.170
I'll miss you too,
Donut Lord.

00:04:50.790 --> 00:04:51.790
Thank you.

00:04:52.529 --> 00:04:53.529
For what?

00:04:54.269 --> 00:04:55.370
For saving my life.

00:05:09.277 --> 00:05:11.898
[ring chimes, warbles]

00:05:14.010 --> 00:05:16.610
Okay. Did someone leave
their "Find My Phone" on?

00:05:17.260 --> 00:05:19.415
[drones whirring]
[gasps]

00:05:24.343 --> 00:05:25.369
[gasps]

